<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/125"><tei:pb n="472" ed="1949 shabbat/minchah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n496_medium.jpg"/><tei:head xml:lang="en">Psalm 125</tei:head><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/125/1"/>A Pilgrim Song. Those who trust in the Lord are like Mount Zion which cannot be shaken, but abides forever. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/125/2"/>The mountains are round about Jerusalem, and the Lord is round about his people, henceforth and forever. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/125/3"/>Verily, the wicked scepter shall not stay in the land of the righteous, or else the righteous themselves might take to evil. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/125/4"/>Do good, O Lord, to those who are good, to those who are upright in heart. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/125/5"/>But as for those who turn to their crooked ways, may the Lord lead them [to destruction] together with the evildoers. Peace be on Israel! <tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p></tei:div>
    </tei:body>
